---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { contact } from '../site';

const hasAnyRoute = Boolean(contact.formUrl || contact.issuesUrl || contact.email);
---
<Base
  title="About — doubleem"
  description="Why the software here is free, what it collects, and who makes it."
>
  <section class="wrap intro">
    <h1>About this place.</h1>
    <p class="intro__lead">
      doubleem is one person putting their work somewhere people can find it. Software
      mostly, for now. What each thing does, and what it costs you, is written on its own
      page — because those answers differ, and a promise made for everything is a promise
      that gets broken.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap prose about">
    <h2>Who makes this</h2>
    <p>
      One person. The work tends to start the same way — someone I know has a problem,
      and the thing that would solve it either does not exist or costs money they should
      not have to spend. The first app here,
      <a href="/apps/logger/">LOGGER</a>, was built with a factory worker in Korea who
      needed to check whether his payslip was right and could not find anything that would
      do it in a language he reads.
    </p>
    <p>
      What turns up here next is not planned. Tools, probably. Possibly writing. It gets
      listed when it works.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site collects</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. No cookies, no analytics, no tracking script, no newsletter box, and no
      email address required to download anything. The pages load no third-party scripts
      at all — even the typeface is served from here rather than from Google. That is why
      you were never shown a consent banner: there is nothing to consent to.
    </p>
    <p>
      What each <em>app</em> collects is a separate question with a separate answer, and it
      is written on that app's own page. LOGGER, for instance, has no server at all.
      Another thing built for another purpose might, and if so it will say so plainly.
    </p>

    <h2>On money</h2>
    <p>
      The apps here are free. For LOGGER that is not only generosity — a free calculator
      that shows its arithmetic is a different thing under Korean law from paid labour
      consulting, and that distinction matters more than the money would.
    </p>
    <p>
      No paid tier, no "pro" version held back, nothing here that is a demo of something
      larger you have to buy.
    </p>

    <h2>Telling me something is wrong</h2>
    <p>
      If something here gives you a wrong number, I want to know. That matters more than
      anything else on this page — LOGGER works out wages, and a figure that is quietly
      wrong is worse than no figure at all. You do not need to be sure it is a bug. "This
      does not match my payslip" is enough to start from.
    </p>

    {hasAnyRoute ? (
      <ul class="routes">
        {contact.formUrl && (
          <li>
            <a href={contact.formUrl}>Report a problem</a> — a short form. No account, no
            sign-up, and it does not go anywhere public.
          </li>
        )}
        {contact.issuesUrl && (
          <li>
            <a href={contact.issuesUrl}>Open an issue on GitHub</a> — public and easier to
            track, if you already have an account.
          </li>
        )}
        {contact.email && (
          <li><a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a></li>
        )}
      </ul>
    ) : (
      <p>There is no way to reach me from this page yet. That is an omission, not a policy.</p>
    )}

    <h2>Why there are no comments or reviews here</h2>
    <p>
      There is nowhere on this site to leave a public comment or a star rating, and that is
      deliberate. Someone checking whether their employer has underpaid them should not
      have to attach their name to it in public, and the feedback worth having — <em>this
      number is wrong</em> — is exactly the kind nobody leaves in a review box.
    </p>
    <p>
      If praise ever appears on this site it will be something a real person said, quoted
      with their permission. Not a widget, and not a number I cannot show you the source of.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { padding-top: clamp(40px, 7vw, 72px); }
  .intro h1 {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 15ch;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 64px);
    font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: var(--track-display); line-height: 1.02;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .intro__lead {
    margin: 22px 0 0;
    max-width: 52ch;
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 21px);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .about { margin-top: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px); }

  .routes { margin: 0 0 1em; padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .routes li { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .routes a { font-weight: 600; }
</style>
